1. d4 { Notes by J. R. Capablanca } 1... d5 2. Nf3 Nf6 3. c4 e6 4. Bg5 Be7 5. e3 Nbd7 6. Nc3 O-O 7. Rc1 Re8 8. Qc2 h6 9. Bh4 c5 10. cxd5 Nxd5 11. Bxe7 Nxe7 12. dxc5 Nxc5 13. Bb5 { Not best. b4 was more
energetic and perfectly safe. } 13... Bd7 14. O-O Qb6 15. Bxd7 Nxd7 16. Rfd1 Red8 17. h3 { Loss of time. Qa4 at once was the proper
move. } 17... Rac8 18. Qa4 Nc6 19. Qb5 a6 20. Qxb6 Nxb6 21. Rxd8+ Nxd8 22. Ne2 Kf8 23. Rxc8 Nxc8 { Not much of a game. With three points
to the good I took matters to easy. My opponent, having the
Black pieces, could not have been expected to do much. } 1/2-1/2

[Event "Lasker - Capablanca World Championship Match"]
[Site "Havana CUB"]
[Date "1921.04.16"]
[Round "12"]
[White "Emanuel Lasker"]
[Black "Jose Raul Capablanca"]
[Result "1/2-1/2"]
[EventDate "?"]
